# What `quarto use template wjschne/apaquarto` leaves out of a new project.
#
# A new project gets the extension (_extensions, which Quarto installs on its
# own), template.qmd renamed after the project, the bibliography it cites,
# and example.qmd with the image it uses. Everything else here is for
# developing apaquarto or for building its website.
#
# Quarto already leaves out dotfiles (.github, .gitignore and the like),
# README.md, LICENSE, CHANGELOG.md and CLAUDE.md. Each line below is a glob
# and is read as written: a comment must go on a line of its own, since a
# trailing "# ..." would leave spaces at the end of the pattern.

# Developing apaquarto
tests
ARCHITECTURE.md
ARCHITECTURE.html
CITATION.cff
DESCRIPTION
Makefile
apaquarto.Rproj
README.qmd
dissertation.qmd
tenzing.R
contributors_table_template_tenzing.xlsx

# The website (docs/ is what it publishes, _freeze/ its cached output)
_quarto.yml
_freeze
docs
site_libs
apaquarto.scss
index.qmd
installation.qmd
apashiny.qmd
options.qmd
options.yml
options-helpers.R
writing.qmd
resources.qmd
changelog.qmd
img
references.bib
apa.csl
apa-cv.csl

